# wip — marker-portability-contracts
# Branch: feature/marker-portability-contracts
# Started: 2026-03-05

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Extend the marker system from a preserved taxonomy into a portable implementation-contract surface. Use the current `family:qualifier` chain as the coarse selector, then design a lightweight metadata layer that helps feature work and ports to other languages without making comments noisy."
 ~#taste: "clarity, correctness, expressiveness"
}

^["stream"]{
 >> [2026-03-05 19:50] observe — the clean post-coverage audit reports 122 markers, but the dominant families remain flat (`todo`, `boundary`, `term`) even after the structured rewrite shipped.
 >> [2026-03-05 19:50] observe — the most useful structured markers today are implementation-adjacent: `portable:seed` (12), `portable:runtime` (3), `boundary:reset` (4), `types:debt` (2), `async:debt` (1).
 >> [2026-03-05 19:50] decide — the next phase should make markers useful for feature execution and language ports, not only for audit inventory.
 >> [2026-03-05 19:50] decide — keep the chain syntax as the stable outer shell and evaluate an optional attribute bag for machine-actionable fields.
 >> [2026-03-05 19:50] taste — the marker surface should stay readable enough to survive hand-authored comments in TS, Rust, Python, Markdown, and `.spw`.
}

^["open"]{
 ?["what attribute syntax best survives TS, Rust, Python, and `.spw` comments without escaping pain?"]
 ?["which contract keys are stable enough to standardize first: target, layer, status, blocker, evidence, owner?"]
 ?["how much fallback normalization is acceptable before the richer contract stops being trustworthy?"]
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[1]: ".[plans] — add marker-portability-contracts plan artifacts"
 ~[2]: "#[marker] — define implementation/port contract fields and syntax candidates"
 ~[3]: "&[marker] — extend marker parser and audit JSON for contract metadata"
 ~[4]: "vocab[marker] — pilot implementation and port markers on seed/runtime surfaces"
 ~[5]: "![marker] — verify contract parsing, filtering, and JSON round-trip"
 ~[6]: ".[docs] — publish implementation and porting guidance for marker contracts"
}

